      <h1 class="article__title">About No Man's Land</h1>
      <p class="article__standfirst">
        Two friends, a domain name, and the stubborn belief that most commentary is written by people
        who have already decided.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="row">
    <div class="rail"></div>
    <div class="body prose">
      <p>
        No man's land is the ground between two positions that nobody has claimed and everybody
        shoots across. That is roughly where we write from. We are not affiliated with a party, a
        publication or a PR budget, and neither of us gets paid for this.
      </p>

      <h2>What we do here</h2>
      <p>
        We pick something that happened, read the primary document instead of the coverage of it, and
        write what we actually think. Sometimes that is a news story. Sometimes it is a regulation
        nobody reported on. Sometimes it is a piece of software or a piece of infrastructure that
        quietly decides something for a lot of people.
      </p>

      <h2>House rules</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Link the source. If we cannot link it, we say where it came from.</li>
        <li>Corrections go at the bottom of the piece, dated, with the original wording intact.</li>
        <li>No anonymous swipes at private people.</li>
        <li>If one of us is wrong in public, the other one says so in public.</li>
      </ul>

